WEBVTT

00:00:10.055 --> 00:00:11.095
(ELASTIGIRL WHOOPS)

00:00:11.335 --> 00:00:12.935
(LAUGHING IN DELIGHT)

00:00:13.815 --> 00:00:15.215
(WHOOPING)

00:00:22.015 --> 00:00:23.135
Wait a minute!

00:00:23.215 --> 00:00:24.575
-Is that Elastigirl?
-I think that's Elastigirl.

00:00:24.735 --> 00:00:26.895
-Hey! Elastigirl!
-(ALL CHEERING)

00:00:33.175 --> 00:00:35.135
MAN: Marry me, Elastigirl!

00:00:37.535 --> 00:00:38.695
WINSTON:
♪ Here comes Elastigirl

00:00:38.775 --> 00:00:39.975
♪ Stretching her ♪

00:00:40.135 --> 00:00:41.295
(LAUGHS) No theme songs

00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:43.455
or I'll turn this bus
right around!

00:00:46.855 --> 00:00:48.295
Look at that.

00:00:48.455 --> 00:00:49.655
New Urbem.

00:00:49.775 --> 00:00:51.495
You wanna make a big
crime fighting statement...

00:00:51.655 --> 00:00:53.335
you go where the crime is big.

00:00:53.495 --> 00:00:55.735
Strange thing to be
excited about, Winston.

00:00:55.895 --> 00:00:58.055
It's like
a superhero's playground!

00:01:00.255 --> 00:01:01.495
(DASH GASPS)

00:01:02.015 --> 00:01:04.095
BOB: No Sugar Bombs
on my watch.

00:01:04.775 --> 00:01:06.135
-(DASH GROANS)
-(JACK-JACK GIGGLES)

00:01:07.495 --> 00:01:08.495
Where's Mom?

00:01:08.655 --> 00:01:09.655
She's up and out.

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:11.375
She's at her new job
doing hero work.

00:01:11.535 --> 00:01:14.055
But I thought superheroes
were still illegal.

00:01:14.255 --> 00:01:15.735
They are, for now.

00:01:15.895 --> 00:01:18.735
So Mom is getting paid
to break the law?

00:01:18.895 --> 00:01:20.135
She's not breaking...

00:01:20.295 --> 00:01:22.535
She's an advocate
for superheroes.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.655
It's a new job.

00:01:23.815 --> 00:01:26.575
So, Mom is going out
illegally...

00:01:26.775 --> 00:01:29.735
to explain why
she shouldn't be illegal.

00:01:29.935 --> 00:01:31.655
Hey... Hey!

00:01:31.815 --> 00:01:33.215
-The bus is here!
-(BUS HORN HONKING)

00:01:33.575 --> 00:01:37.215
Whoa! Grab your stuff quickly!
Go on, get on the...

00:01:38.055 --> 00:01:40.175
Put your homework
in your pack!

00:01:41.175 --> 00:01:42.335
Bye-bye!

00:01:44.095 --> 00:01:45.535
(EXHALES)

00:01:45.615 --> 00:01:47.135
(JACK-JACK GIGGLING)

00:01:48.375 --> 00:01:50.855
We're gonna get along
just fine...

00:01:51.015 --> 00:01:52.895
'cause you don't ask
any hard questions.

00:01:52.975 --> 00:01:54.055
(STOMACH GROWLING)

00:01:54.135 --> 00:01:55.295
(THUDS)

00:01:55.535 --> 00:01:56.855
-(GIGGLES)
-(SIGHS)

00:01:56.935 --> 00:01:58.455
OFFICER 1:
All right. All locations,

00:01:58.535 --> 00:01:59.535
we need to know
where you want us.

00:01:59.695 --> 00:02:00.735
OFFICER 2: Stand by.

00:02:00.815 --> 00:02:03.895
Seems strange
to wait for crime.

00:02:04.095 --> 00:02:05.655
WINSTON: Relax.
You're smack in the middle...

00:02:05.815 --> 00:02:09.095
of the worst crime area
in the city. It's perfect.

00:02:09.255 --> 00:02:10.575
It's a superhero's playground.

00:02:10.655 --> 00:02:12.215
"It's a superhero's
playground." Right.

00:02:12.375 --> 00:02:14.015
You know,
after we went underground...

00:02:14.175 --> 00:02:15.855
my husband used to listen
to a police scanner...

00:02:16.015 --> 00:02:17.495
waiting for something
to happen.

00:02:17.695 --> 00:02:19.375
And I got mad at him for it.

00:02:19.575 --> 00:02:21.015
(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:02:21.335 --> 00:02:22.735
Oh, I'm such a hypocrite.

00:02:23.055 --> 00:02:24.295
-DISPATCHER: All units.
-Something's up.

00:02:24.495 --> 00:02:25.535
We've been picking up
some chatter about

00:02:25.615 --> 00:02:28.615
potential disruptions to the
hovertrain's opening ceremony.

00:02:29.375 --> 00:02:31.415
OFFICER: Disruption or threat?
DISPATCHER: Both.

00:02:31.575 --> 00:02:32.895
Station's at Fifty-Fourth
and Nottingham.

00:02:32.975 --> 00:02:34.975
(GASPS) A potential threat!
Perfect!

00:02:35.175 --> 00:02:37.455
Fifty-fourth and Nottingham.
Go, go, go!

00:02:39.255 --> 00:02:42.495
Hey, Vi! I want you back here
by 10:30.

00:02:42.575 --> 00:02:43.615
11-ish?

00:02:43.695 --> 00:02:45.895
10-ish, heading for 9:30-ish.

00:02:46.055 --> 00:02:48.055
10:30-ish it is. (SIGHS)

00:02:48.135 --> 00:02:49.535
Enjoy the movie.

00:02:49.695 --> 00:02:51.735
"In the county of Noddoff...

00:02:51.895 --> 00:02:53.855
"the Frubbers of Freep...

00:02:54.015 --> 00:02:58.775
"are all giving in
to the sweet succor of sleep."

00:03:06.735 --> 00:03:08.095
(SIGHS)

00:03:08.495 --> 00:03:10.895
VIC PERRIN: (ON TV) We will
control the horizontal...

00:03:11.055 --> 00:03:13.055
we will control the vertical.

00:03:19.255 --> 00:03:22.335
That's not the way
you're supposed to do it, Dad.

00:03:22.495 --> 00:03:24.135
They want us
to do it this way.

00:03:24.295 --> 00:03:27.095
I don't know that way!
Why would they change math?

00:03:27.255 --> 00:03:29.455
-It's okay, Dad.
-Math is math!

00:03:29.615 --> 00:03:31.455
I'll just wait for Mom
to get back.

00:03:31.535 --> 00:03:32.535
What?

00:03:32.615 --> 00:03:34.655
She won't understand it
any better than I do...

00:03:35.575 --> 00:03:36.815
VIC PERRIN: (ON TV)
The Outer Limits.

00:03:38.695 --> 00:03:39.935
(JACK-JACK GIGGLES)

00:03:40.015 --> 00:03:41.575
"All over Doozle-Dorf,

00:03:41.655 --> 00:03:43.935
"the Fribbers of Frupp
are going to sleep...

00:03:44.095 --> 00:03:46.175
"'cause they just
can't keep up.

00:03:46.335 --> 00:03:49.935
"All over Doozle-Dorf,
Doozles are dozing.

00:03:50.095 --> 00:03:54.415
"Eyelids so heavy,
they're drooping.

00:03:54.495 --> 00:03:55.655
(BOB SNORES)

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.655
"Closing! The point is:

00:03:57.735 --> 00:04:00.135
"Everyone,
everyone's hitting the sack!

00:04:00.295 --> 00:04:03.535
"Everyone's getting the sleep
that they lack."

00:04:03.655 --> 00:04:06.815
Mayors often brag
about their cities...

00:04:07.015 --> 00:04:08.495
(CHUCKLES)
and I'm no exception.

00:04:08.655 --> 00:04:09.895
And I'm willing to admit

00:04:10.015 --> 00:04:12.055
that New Urbem
is not the only city...

00:04:12.335 --> 00:04:14.415
Are you sure the police are
gonna be okay with this?

00:04:14.535 --> 00:04:16.375
EVELYN: Sure. You're making
life easy for them.

00:04:16.535 --> 00:04:17.655
They still haven't forgiven us

00:04:17.775 --> 00:04:19.335
for the last time we made
life easy for them.

00:04:19.495 --> 00:04:21.495
I know the Chief of Police.
There won't be a problem.

00:04:21.695 --> 00:04:22.815
With all due respect...

00:04:22.975 --> 00:04:25.055
if you alone had handled
the Underminer...

00:04:25.215 --> 00:04:26.895
things would have
been different.

00:04:27.215 --> 00:04:28.375
I'm just saying.

00:04:28.575 --> 00:04:30.775
MAYOR: ...on budget
and ahead of schedule...

00:04:30.935 --> 00:04:34.215
to launch our magnificent
new hovertrain.

00:04:34.415 --> 00:04:36.815
It can get you
where you need to go

00:04:36.895 --> 00:04:38.935
at ridiculous speeds.

00:04:39.095 --> 00:04:42.255
The future is open
for business!

00:04:42.535 --> 00:04:43.815
-(MARCHING BAND PLAYING)
-(PEOPLE CHEERING)

00:04:51.815 --> 00:04:52.935
(GRUNTS)

00:04:56.575 --> 00:04:58.215
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:05:02.455 --> 00:05:03.775
Wait. The train has stopped.

00:05:03.935 --> 00:05:04.935
(PEOPLE GASP)

00:05:07.495 --> 00:05:08.615
It's going
the wrong direction.

00:05:10.175 --> 00:05:11.575
It's going the wrong way.

00:05:11.735 --> 00:05:12.735
I'm going after it.

00:05:17.815 --> 00:05:20.055
-(PEOPLE CLAMORING)
-This thing's really moving.

00:05:20.215 --> 00:05:22.495
100 and climbing.
How much track is built?

00:05:23.895 --> 00:05:25.175
EVELYN: About 25 miles.

00:05:32.735 --> 00:05:34.855
(GRUNTS) No one can shut
this thing down?

00:05:35.015 --> 00:05:36.015
EVELYN: They've tried. No-go.

00:05:38.255 --> 00:05:39.535
Is that Elastigirl?

00:05:42.335 --> 00:05:44.015
-(SIRENS WAILING)
-(BOTH GASP)

00:05:45.295 --> 00:05:46.535
(BRAKES SCREECHING)

00:05:47.255 --> 00:05:48.255
Overrides?

00:05:48.335 --> 00:05:49.495
They're locked out
of the system.

00:05:54.655 --> 00:05:56.255
(ELASTIGIRL GRUNTING)

00:05:56.695 --> 00:05:58.815
-What about a fail-safe?
-EVELYN: Not enough time.

00:05:59.015 --> 00:06:00.855
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:03.855
Someone's calling!
Switching over.

00:06:04.015 --> 00:06:05.815
DASH: Hey, Mom.
I can't find my high-tops

00:06:05.895 --> 00:06:06.935
and Dad
can't find them either.

00:06:07.095 --> 00:06:09.535
But he won't call you and ask,
so I am.

00:06:09.695 --> 00:06:11.015
BOB: Do not call your mother!

00:06:11.175 --> 00:06:12.615
Dash, honey.
Can't talk right now.

00:06:12.775 --> 00:06:14.575
Look under your bed, okay.
How much time?

00:06:14.655 --> 00:06:15.655
EVELYN:
Less than two minutes!

00:06:16.615 --> 00:06:18.415
There's a shortcut. Cut
through the culvert up ahead.

00:06:26.815 --> 00:06:28.935
I don't know
if I can stay with it.

00:06:30.775 --> 00:06:32.015
(YELLS)

00:06:35.655 --> 00:06:36.935
(GRUNTS)

00:06:39.775 --> 00:06:41.135
(ENGINE REVVING)

00:06:47.815 --> 00:06:49.255
(GRUNTING)

00:06:58.615 --> 00:06:59.735
(ALL GASP)

00:07:04.055 --> 00:07:05.215
(GASPING)

00:07:23.255 --> 00:07:24.375
(GRUNTS)

00:07:27.015 --> 00:07:28.855
(GASPS AND GRUNTS)

00:07:37.055 --> 00:07:38.375
(GRUNTING)

